-Both H3 aliases now accept only `text_to_video`/`t2v` at HTTP submission. The native LightX2V runner also contains `t2av`, `i2av`, `l2av`, `fl2av` and `ref2av` code, but public reference media is not wired; `input` accepts only `prompt` and media fields are rejected before queueing. The shared API includes the newer Krea2/SeedVR2 integrations; H3 kernel optimization evidence is recorded separately.
+Both H3 aliases accept `text_to_video`/`t2v` and `ref2av`. Reference files are uploaded through `/v1/files` and passed by `file_id`. The native runner uses TP6 for text-to-video and TP4 for reference generation because the 56-head `transformer_ref` partition does not divide evenly across six ranks. See `API.md` for the public reference input rules and limits. The shared API also includes the Krea2/SeedVR2 integrations; H3 kernel optimization evidence is recorded separately.
 
 The installed native H3 reference packer has ceilings of 9 images, 3 videos, 3 audio-bearing references and 12 total references. Audio-only bundles are rejected; a soundtrack on a reference video consumes one audio-bearing slot. These are implementation ceilings, not a public API contract or a six-V100 capacity guarantee. See [the full API manual](../AIserver/API.md#原生-h3-全能参考上限尚未开放为-http-参数).
 
